description:
FOUND by s539d (#233) while probing caller(); PRE-EXISTING on main 05806e16 (probed on the extraction), unchanged by s539d.  SILENT WRONG (a diagnostic, and the target package of a caller-driven import).

    sub show { join "|", @_ }
    sub f11 { my @c = caller(0); print show(@c[0..3]), "\n" }
    my $obj = bless {}, 'K'; sub K::m { main::f11() } $obj->m;

    perl:  main|p.pl|3|main::f11
    PCL:   k|...|main::f11

TWO faces, ONE place: p-sub's per-sub constant %%home-pkg = (pcl-pkg-perl-name (symbol-package local-sym)), the package of the sub's NAME symbol.  (1) perl's code inside `sub K::m {...}` runs in the package it was COMPILED in (CopSTASH = main), not the package the name is installed in; (2) the CL package of a single-segment Perl package that no `package K;` statement ever named reads through :invert as "k", and *pcl-pkg-name-map* has no entry for it, so the case is lost too.  Fix shape: the emitter knows the compiling package of every `sub NAME` and could hand it to p-sub (a FACT, only on a QUALIFIED sub name, so a few bytes per such sub) -- measure.  Probe: s539d scratch pr/p1.pl row J.
